! mcp_bootstrap_p181.strap -- "CONTROL WORD CHECK", the routine two
! other landed decks have been branching into for a fortnight without
! its defining page: printed page 181.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.188 (printed + 7).  The title line
! was READ at 300 dpi, not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP  CARD ID LB000001  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER  181".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK. <<<
! Rendered at 300 dpi (crop x=3300 y=150 W=1800 H=150 of the 300-dpi
! page): the word "LOCATION" is printed at the right-hand end of the
! heading row and NOTHING follows it -- clean paper from the word to
! the table's right rule.  No digits were taken off the dashed rule
! and none were taken from the survey OCR.  That is the case
! docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1 predicts: the field is LINE
! 1'S location, and line 1 here is an asterisk banner that compiles
! nothing.  A blank is NOT a zero and it is NOT "this page has no
! origin"; see the origin note below for what does establish it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES.  Lines 1-3 are an asterisk banner
! ("-************** CONTROL WORD CHECK **************-"), lines 4-54
! are fifty-one emitting rows of straight code, lines 55-56 are two
! SYN cards.  No SLC, no DD, no VF, no DR/DRZ reservation, no EXT, no
! entry-mode card, no I-O pseudo-op anywhere on the page.
!
! THE CODE IS CONTIGUOUS FROM 221102.00 TO 221144.00 AND HAS NO HOLE.
! Eighteen of the fifty-one rows are full words (the BINARY OUTPUT
! column prints TWO half words) and thirty-three are half words:
!
!     18 * 2  +  33 * 1   =   69 half words
!     221144.40 - 221102.00 = 0o42 words + 0o40 bits
!                           = 34 words + 32 bits = 69 half words
!
! The two counts are computed from DIFFERENT things -- the first from
! how many half words each row's BINARY OUTPUT column prints, the
! second from the first and last LOCATION -- and they agree exactly,
! so NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END and no row is missing in the middle.
! The per-row walk agrees too: every location is its predecessor plus
! that predecessor's own width, fifty times running.
!
! >>> SO THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 221144.40. <<<  Line 54 is a
! HALF word at 221144.00.  See the prediction for printed p.182 at the
! foot of this header: 221144.40 is Z STEVL, and TEN landed decks
! already SYN it there, all ten at the same value.
!
! CARD SERIALS: LB000001 through LB000052, consecutive, with FOUR
! serials printed TWICE -- LB000015 (lines 15/16), LB000023 (24/25),
! LB000031 (33/34) and LB000050 (53/54).  52 cards, 56 lines, 4
! repeats: 52 + 4 = 56.  Every one of the four repeats is a
! "SIC,<save>; B,<entry>" PAIR on ONE card, the two-statement card
! C22-6728 quotes as "(SIC,STIC; B,SIFAD)".  The first serial is on
! line 1 and the last is on line 56, so nothing is lost at either
! edge of the form.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE ROUTINE DOES, off the page's own English
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! B CWCR (line 4) is the entry.  It saves the IC's return in JPICK,
! branches away if the control word belongs to MCP (line 5, "BB,SL" --
! S L is the LEVEL OF INSTRUCTION bit), and otherwise CHECKS THE CW's
! ADDRESS against the problem program's bounds: lines 8/9 load S UPPER
! and subtract S LOWER (comment "-CHECK IF ADDR. OF CW"), lines 12/13
! set those same bounds into $R as the page's own private pair S LOWA
! / S UPPB (lines 55/56, which are SYNs INTO $R, not storage), and
! lines 49/50 are the test itself -- KF/KFR against S LOWA and S UPPB,
! comments "-TEST ADDR. FOR" / "-RANGE".
!
! JMORCW (line 14) is the per-control-word loop head: fetch the CW
! address, SIC/B through JADOUT/JADIN to range-check it, load the
! actual CW (line 17), test its SKIP bit (18), its READ bit (21), its
! DISK bit (35), its MULTI bit (29, "-TEST MULTI BIT"), and its CHAIN
! (36-38, "-CHAINING" / "-CHAINED ADDR." / "-END OF CHAIN"), then loop
! with CB,$0,JMORCW (39).  JPICK (43-47) builds the control word
! that goes to the FAT slots, S CW and S CCW.  BCWERR (52) is the
! error exit: LVI,$14,S CWINV then SIC,S DISIC; B,S DISP.
!
! B1RA (line 48) is a one-row trampoline, "B,$" with the comment
! "-EXIT PRESET BY SIC" -- a branch to itself that the SIC on the
! caller's side overwrites.  printed pp.151 and 153 both print
! "SIC,B1RA" immediately followed by "B,B CWCR", which is this
! page's entry and this page's trampoline used as one pair.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE DEFINES TWO OF THE MERGED BODY'S UNRESOLVED
! EXTERNALS, AND BOTH WERE PREDICTED BY OTHER PAGES' INK. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Before this page landed the merge of printed pp.99-176 carried 62
! external symbols.  Eight of them lie in 0o2211xx; two are here:
!
!   BCWCR  221102.00   line 4 ("B CWC R" on the page)   -- decks p.151 and p.153 both carry
!                                   "BCWCR SYN, (8)221102.0", read off
!                                   their own printed "B,B CWCR" rows
!                                   compiling 221102.10 00.
!   B1RA   221140.00   line 48 ("B1RA", closed up)  -- decks p.151 and p.153 both carry
!                                   "B1RA SYN, (8)221140.0", read off
!                                   their printed "SIC,B1RA" rows
!                                   compiling 221140.00 80.  A SIC's
!                                   half word carries the operand's
!                                   FULL 24-bit bit address (Reference
!                                   Manual printed p.41), so those two
!                                   rows pin B1RA TO THE BIT, and this
!                                   page's LOCATION column agrees with
!                                   them digit for digit.
!
! THAT IS A GENUINELY INDEPENDENT WITNESS FOR THIS PAGE'S ORIGIN and
! it is not the volume OCR: p.151 and p.153 are different cards, at
! different locations, on different pages, transcribed by different
! people, and their value was fixed before anyone opened p.188 of the
! PDF.  It is what turns "221102.00 is what I read" into "221102.00 is
! what two other pages' machine code says it must be".
!
! The other six 0o2211xx externals are NOT on this page and belong to
! printed p.182 and after: Z STEVL 221144.40, Z EVLMK 221152.00,
! E MK1A 221152.40, R MASK 221153.00, Z EVLRW 221153.40, R VFY
! 221161.00.  All six are above this page's last word.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN IS ASSERTED BY THE DECK AND CORROBORATED, NOT PRINTED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints NO "SLC,$", so the free forward-join witness that
! docs/transcription_workflow.md prizes is not on offer here.  The
! deck therefore writes a HARD "SLC,(8)221102." and that SLC CANNOT
! FAIL -- it overrides the arriving counter silently (workflow, "WHAT
! THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" item 2).  What stops it being a bare
! assertion is the paragraph above: pp.151/153 independently place
! B CWCR, this page's line 4, at 221102.0.
!
! >>> FALSIFIABLE PREDICTION FOR printed p.180: its counter must
! LEAVE at 221102.00. <<<  If p.180's last row plus its own width is
! anything else, one of the two pages is wrong and this deck's SLC is
! hiding it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THIS DECK DISAGREES WITH THE CACHED SURVEY, AND WHY IT WINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The survey reports this page as "222102.0".."221132.40", endpoints
! out of order, so at least one had to be a misread.  Both are:
!
!   * "222102.0" is 221102.00 with the third digit lost.  Settled by
!     the 600-dpi LOCATION crop AND by pp.151/153's SYN above.
!   * "221132.40" is line 42, not the last row.  That is not a random
!     truncation -- `python3 strap/mcp_ocr.py 181` reads 27 of 56 rows
!     and its LAST successful row is line 42, 221132.40, exactly the
!     survey's endpoint.  The survey inherits mcp_ocr's window and
!     stops where it stops.  The page runs twelve rows further, to
!     221144.00.
!   * The survey also cannot tell a LOCATION from a SYMBOL VALUE.
!     Lines 55 and 56 print "000011.32+" and "000011.55+"; the
!     TRAILING PLUS says those are values of S LOWA and S UPPB, not
!     addresses, and the location counter never visits word 0o11.
!     They are correctly absent from the span above.
!
! All twenty-seven locations mcp_ocr DID read agree with the eye
! reading here, digit for digit, except line 40 where it returns
! "221131.46" for a printed 221131.40.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND BY WHICH RUNG OF THE LADDER
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * LINE 6's MNEMONIC IS "CT0011", NOT "CTOO11".  The two round
!   glyphs after CT are wide and closed and look exactly like the
!   letter O.  Rung 3 (the assembler as ELIMINATOR) is decisive:
!   strap_asm's classify_connective takes C/CM/CT plus EXACTLY FOUR
!   BINARY DIGITS (X22-6533 "CONNECTIVES"), so "CTOO11" is not an
!   operation at all and "CT0011" is.  The field can hold only 0 and
!   1, which is rung 5 pointing the same way.
! * LINE 11's SECOND OPERAND IS "$X0", NOT "$XC".  Same argument from
!   the other side: "$N"/"$XN" takes N = 0-15, so a C cannot stand
!   there.  And the row CHECKS it -- $X0 in an address field is index
!   register 0 at word 0o20, and the printed half word is
!   "000020.02 30".  A "$XC" could not produce 000020.
! * "JADOUT", NOT "J ADCUT" (lines 24, 33, 51).  Line 24 and line 33
!   print the same statement; line 33's O is CLOSED and line 24's is
!   OPEN, in the same character position on one page off one drum.
!   That is rung 4, the strongest rung.  Line 51's NAME column prints
!   it closed as well, and the page's English ("-ADDR OF CW", JADIN /
!   JADOUT as a pair) agrees.
! * LINE 4's BYTE IS "D0" AND LINE 7's IS "C0".  Both read as a round
!   glyph plus a round glyph at 400 dpi.  At 900 dpi line 4's first
!   character has a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT STEM and squared corners
!   and line 7's does not -- the C/D discriminator of
!   docs/transcription_workflow.md.  Both are then CHECKED by the
!   oracle below, which is what actually settles them.
! * LINE 42's BYTE IS "3C", not "30".  Settled on WHAT PRODUCED IT:
!   the low nibble of an indexed half word is the index, and the
!   statement is "SV,0,3.32($12)" -- 12 is 0xC.
! * LINE 45's ADDRESS IS "-1.09", with a 9.  Settled by arithmetic,
!   not ink: -(64+9) bits as a 24-bit bit address is 16777143, which
!   is word 0o777776 bit 0o67, and the page prints "777776.67".  No
!   other low digit gives that.
! * THE OCTAL FIELDS DROP INK CONSTANTLY on this page -- "COOO11.CC"
!   for 000011.00 on line 10, "007000.C7" for 007000.07 on line 6,
!   "215001.C4" for 215001.04 on line 5.  An octal field cannot hold a
!   C, so each of those is a damaged 0 with certainty.  That is rung 5
!   and it is used ONLY to show the page can drop ink; it licenses
!   nothing about a particular hex byte (workflow: ink varies per
!   CHARACTER, not per row).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK: THREE OF THEM, AND NO RULE PROPOSED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A second asterisk appears after the LOCATION on lines 13
! (221111.00), 32 (221125.00) and 49 (221140.40).  Recorded and left
! alone, as docs/transcription_workflow.md instructs.
!
! The tempting hypothesis -- "a full-word VFL row carrying BOTH a dds
! AND a trailing offset" -- fits all three of mine and is DEAD ON
! ARRIVAL: decks/mcp_bootstrap_p176.strap records its two asterisks at
! 220651.00 and 220664.00, and both are "SIC,STIC", half word, no dds,
! no offset.  So that is not the rule, and this page proposes none.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT RESTS ON INK ALONE, AND IS THE HONEST EDGE OF "BIT-EXACT"
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! listing_oracle checks LOCATIONS and BINARY and never label
! SPELLINGS.  B CWCR and B1RA are safe -- other pages reference them
! and the merge would refuse an undefined symbol.  These nine are
! referenced ONLY from inside this page, so their spelling is read off
! this drum and nothing can fail if it is wrong:
!
!     JMORCW  JJSKP  JJSKP1  JDISCK  JPICK  JPICK1
!     JADIN   JADOUT  BCWERR
!
! Each was read at 900 dpi and each is printed at least twice on the
! page (once in the NAME column, once or more in a statement), so the
! within-page cross-check is as strong as it can be made here; it is
! still one drum.  S LOWA and S UPPB (lines 55/56) are in the same
! position, with the extra comfort that their VALUES are checked:
! lines 49 and 50 print 000011.32 and 000011.55 as their operands.
!
! WHICH NAMES CARRY A PRINTED BLANK, MEASURED BY CHARACTER PITCH AT
! 1800 dpi AND NOT GUESSED.  ALL THIRTEEN NAME-column entries were
! rendered at 1800 dpi for this, in five crops of x=13900..16100
! (y = 2960, 4300, 9000, 13700 and 18100, heights 330-4700).  The
! drum's pitch there is 180 px; a blank is one whole empty cell and
! is unmistakable.  EXACTLY THREE of the thirteen carry one:
!
!     line  4   "B CWC R"   B, blank, CWC, blank, R  -> BCWCR
!     line 55   "S LOWA"    S, blank, LOWA           -> SLOWA
!     line 56   "S UPPB"    S, blank, UPPB           -> SUPPB
!
! The other ten -- JMORCW, JJSKP, JJSKP1, JDISCK, JPICK1, JPICK,
! B1RA, JADIN, JADOUT, BCWERR -- are printed CLOSED UP at regular
! pitch, every one checked in the same five crops.  (A first draft of this deck wrote them all with a blank by
! analogy with the operand column and was wrong; the pitch
! measurement is what corrected it.)  B1RA's second glyph is the
! DIGIT 1, which at 1800 dpi has both the upper-left flag and the
! base serif that this drum's capital I lacks -- the reading decks
! p.151 and p.153 already carry, now confirmed on the DEFINING page.
!
! FIVE OPERANDS DO carry a printed blank -- "L(BU,18),S UPPER" (12),
! "LF(BU,18),S LOWER,19" (13), "BB,$1.26,BCW ERR" (29), "SIC,S DISIC"
! (53) and "B,S DISP" (54) -- and all five are written EXACTLY as
! printed in the deck above and all five assemble, because STRAP
! ignores a blank inside a name and this assembler accepts one in an
! OPERAND.  It REFUSES one in the NAME field, which is why the three
! blanked NAMES are written closed up:
!
!     "B CWC R SVA,$0,JPICK"  ->  unknown mnemonic 'CWCRSVA'
!     "S LOWA  SYN,$R.26"     ->  unknown mnemonic 'LOWASYN'
!
! That is the known gap the brief names, re-measured here, not worked
! around silently: the printed blanks are recorded in the listing
! block at the foot of this file.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FALSIFIABLE PREDICTION FOR printed p.182 <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! It begins at 221144.40, and its first located row carries the NAME
! "Z STEVL".  TEN landed decks -- pp.151, 152, 153, 156, 159, 160,
! 162, 163, 164 and 165, counted with grep, every one writing the
! SAME value -- SYN ZSTEVL at (8)221144.40 off their printed
! "B,Z STEVL" rows
! compiling "221144.50 00", and p.160's deck quotes a volume-OCR
! fragment of the DEFINING row as "221144.40  000002.54 3C  Z STEVL".
! This page's counter leaves at exactly 221144.40, so the two meet
! with no gap.  If p.182 opens anywhere else, this deck is wrong.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  Every one is SYN'd to the value the page that PRINTS
! its defining card establishes, spelled the way the landed decks
! spell it so the merge compares like with like.  None is a verbatim
! copy of a defining card (workflow: a copy COLLIDES, a stand-in is
! CHECKED).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0             ! the DEFINING card is decks/mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap line 260, "STLR DRZ(BU,64), 29", its own line 13 (checked with grep: p.116 is the only deck in the corpus carrying a DRZ for this name); 14 landed decks SYN it at this value
SUPPER  SYN, STLR                    ! printed p.116 line 14 -PP UPPER BOUNDRY
SLOWER  SYN, STLR+0.32               ! printed p.116 line 15
SL      SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.04      ! printed p.103 line 14 -LEVEL OF INSTR; the (BU,1) dds is the defining page's
SCW     SYN(BU,64), 3.0              ! printed p.102 line 14 -CONTROL WORD
SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! printed p.102 line 15 -COPIED CONTROL WORD
SCWINV  SYN,(16)1007.0               ! printed p.107 line 12 -7 CW INVALID; p.107's !SYM is 010007.00
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! printed p.103; four landed decks
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! printed p.103; five landed decks

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE.  Lines 1-3 are the banner; lines 4-54 are below in
! printed order; lines 55-56 are the two SYN cards, left where the
! page prints them.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

        SLC,(8)221102.

BCWCR   SVA,$0,JPICK                 ! line  4  printed "B CWC R"   -ADDR OF CW
        BB,SL,JPICK1                 ! line  5                      -BRANCH IF MCP
        CT0011(BU,7),$X0+.18         ! line  6                      -CHECK IF ADDR. OF CW
        BZRZ,BCWERR                  ! line  7
        L(BU,18),SUPPER,46           ! line  8
        -(BU,18),SLOWER,46           ! line  9
        LC,$0,$R                     ! line 10                      -MAX NO OF CONTROL WORDS
        LV,$1,$X0                    ! line 11
        L(BU,18),S UPPER             ! line 12                      -SET BOUNDS IN $R
        LF(BU,18),S LOWER,19         ! line 13  (LOCATION asterisk)
JMORCW  LF(BU,18),$1,38              ! line 14  printed "JMORCW"   -CW ADDR.
        SIC,JADOUT                   ! line 15  card LB000015, statement 1
        B,JADIN                      ! line 16  card LB000015, statement 2
        LX,$1,0.0($1)                ! line 17                      -ACTUAL CW
        BZB,$1.27,JJSKP              ! line 18                      -IF NO SKIP BIT
        KVI,4,.32                    ! line 19
        BXE,JJSKP                    ! line 20
        KVI,$3,1.0                   ! line 21                      -READ = 1.0
        BXE,JDISCK                   ! line 22
JJSKP   LF(BU,18),$1,38              ! line 23  printed "JJSKP"    -GET 1ST ADDRESS
        SIC,JADOUT                   ! line 24  card LB000023, statement 1
        B,JADIN                      ! line 25  card LB000023, statement 2
        SC,$1,$6                     ! line 26                      -COMPUTE
        BZXCZ,JJSKP1                 ! line 27                      -LASTADDRESS WHEN UNDER
        KVI,4,.32                    ! line 28                      -BLOCK CONTROL
        BB,$1.26,BCW ERR             ! line 29  printed WITH the blank  -TEST MULTI BIT
        BXE,BCWERR                   ! line 30                      -BR IF DISK CW IS ZERO
JJSKP1  V-I,6,1.                     ! line 31  printed "JJSKP1"
        +(BU,18),$6,38               ! line 32  (LOCATION asterisk) -BLOCK CONTROL
        SIC,JADOUT                   ! line 33  card LB000031, statement 1
        B,JADIN                      ! line 34  card LB000031, statement 2
JDISCK  KVI,$4,.32                   ! line 35  printed "JDISCK"   -IF DISK, NO
        BXE,JPICK1                   ! line 36                      -CHAINING
        SR,$1,$1                     ! line 37                      -CHAINED ADDR.
        BZXF,JPICK1                  ! line 38                      -END OF CHAIN
        CB,$0,JMORCW                 ! line 39
JPICK1  LV,0,$13                     ! line 40  printed "JPICK1"
        V+I,0,3.                     ! line 41
        SV,0,3.32($12)               ! line 42                      -CW ADD IN FET TO LAT
JPICK   LF(BU,64),$                  ! line 43  printed "JPICK"    -INITIAL CW
        LFI(BU,6),(2)100000,40       ! line 44                      -SET STATUS BITS
        LF(BU,1),-1.09($2),39        ! line 45                      -SEOP BIT
        SF(BU,64),SCW($13)           ! line 46                      -CW TO FAT SLOTS
        SF(BU,64),SCCW($13)          ! line 47
B1RA    B,$                          ! line 48  printed "B1RA"     -EXIT PRESET BY SIC
JADIN   KF(BU,19),SLOWA,38           ! line 49  printed "JADIN"; (LOCATION asterisk)  -TEST ADDR. FOR
        KFR(BU,19),SUPPB,38          ! line 50                      -RANGE
JADOUT  BAE,$                        ! line 51  printed "JADOUT"   -AE WHEN OK
BCWERR  LVI,$14,SCWINV               ! line 52  printed "BCWERR"
        SIC,S DISIC                  ! line 53  card LB000050, statement 1
        B,S DISP                     ! line 54  card LB000050, statement 2
SLOWA   SYN,$R.26                    ! line 55  printed "S LOWA"; value 000011.32+
SUPPB   SYN,$R.45                    ! line 56  printed "S UPPB"; value 000011.55+

